From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dreyk <dreyksmail@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:11:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] device: set the offload device before attaching

At startup bridger removes the offload filters that an earlier instance
left behind: every device found before init is marked for cleanup, and
attaching a bridge port clears its offload priorities and those of its
offload chain. __device_update() attaches the port before it looks up
the offload device, so the chain is still empty at that point and the
conduit (e.g. eth0 under a DSA port), where the flower rules actually
are, is never cleaned.

After bridger was killed and restarted by procd, the rule of an active
flow stayed in hardware and the new instance did not know about it. When
the client then moved to another port (5 GHz -> 2.4 GHz), the PPE kept
forwarding the flow to the old port: 44 s without traffic on the client,
until it came back to 5 GHz.

Look up the offload device before attaching.
---
 device.c | 15 ++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/device.c b/device.c
index fd63137..351a125 100644
--- a/device.c
+++ b/device.c
@@ -403,17 +403,22 @@ static void __device_update(struct device *dev)
 
 	dev->master = master;
 
-	attach = (dev->master || dev->br) && !bridger_ubus_dev_blacklisted(dev);
-	device_set_attached(dev, attach);
-	bridger_bpf_dev_policy_set(dev);
-	device_set_tx_attached(dev, attach && dev->redirect_dev);
-
+	/*
+	 * Set the offload device first: attaching cleans up the offload
+	 * filters that an earlier instance left on the device and on its
+	 * offload chain, and the chain must be known for that.
+	 */
 	odev = device_get_offload_dev(dev);
 	if (odev != dev->offload_dev)
 		D("Set device %s offload device to %s\n", dev->ifname,
 		  odev ? odev->ifname : "(none)");
 
 	dev->offload_dev = odev;
+
+	attach = (dev->master || dev->br) && !bridger_ubus_dev_blacklisted(dev);
+	device_set_attached(dev, attach);
+	bridger_bpf_dev_policy_set(dev);
+	device_set_tx_attached(dev, attach && dev->redirect_dev);
 }
 
 static void bridger_device_update_cb(struct uloop_timeout *t)
-- 
